title Spike 6: logging out entrenches
about Blue's player logs out: the army digs in as turrets and holds the line against red's waves. They log back in: the turrets mobilize and push.

scenario skirmish
units 0
respawn off
bot blue off
bot red off
clip 0..1200
camera 250,256 110

# Blue holds a line of tanks. The player logs out at 2 s: the server
# entrenches them (logout policy "entrench"), and turrets outrange raiders
# and tanks alike.
at 0    spawn blue tank 12 at 210,256 radius 8
at 60   entrench blue

# Red's waves, from the east, while nobody is at the controls.
at 90   spawn red raider 12 at 330,240 radius 8
at 90   spawn red tank 3 at 285,272 radius 6
at 92   select red any within 60 of 310,256 as wave1
at 93   attack-move wave1 200,256
at 450  spawn red raider 12 at 330,240 radius 8
at 450  spawn red tank 3 at 285,272 radius 6
at 452  select red any within 60 of 310,256 as wave2
at 453  attack-move wave2 200,256

# The player is back: the turrets turn into tanks again and go after what's left.
at 840  mobilize blue
at 842  select blue tank as army
at 843  attack-move army 330,256

at 62   expect blue turrets == 12
at 830  expect blue lost <= 4        # observed 3 of 12
at 830  expect red lost >= 24        # observed 26 of 30, before blue is back
at 1190 expect blue tanks >= 7       # observed 8
at 1190 expect red units == 0
